A||N||4||Vlad||Bad Gas Mileage...(Need advise)||||13||
Z||000000||Vlad||09-09-2000||01:35 AM||||Hello.<P>My gas mileage is really bad. About 15 mpg city/highway driving. No heavy foot. I've had it since I bought my Fiero (about 1 month ago) and since then getting 15 miles to the gallon. Exhaust smells very rich.<P>I have put on new wires, pickup coil, plugs, air filter, O2 sensor, and dis cap. Didn't help.<BR> <BR>From time to time during hard accelerations and while driving with highway speeds, I get cod 32.=&gt; EGR valve is OK. No vacuum leaks.<BR>I suspect an EGR solenoid.<P>Also, I'm going to replace a ECM coolant sensor. Got one for free off dead 87 Fiero 4 cil. (Just to confirm. I took that sensor from thermostat housing. The sensor was pointed toward the rear of the car. Is it the right coolant temp sensor?)<P>Another reason for bad mileage, I may suspect, is the wide tires on my car. They are 235/60 R14.<P>Any input about this situation  highly appreciated.<P><BR>||||reg||13
Z||000001||Vlad||09-09-2000||01:53 AM||||And one more thing.<P>What cars have the same EGR solenoid as V6 Fiero? <P>So I will know what to look for when I come to the boneyard.<P>Vlad <BR>85 GT V6 auto||||reg||5
Z||000002||88formula||09-09-2000||08:21 PM||||Does your car have good vacuum, 18-20 inches at idle? Do you have an exhaust manifold leak? Are your injectors clogged and leaking? If so send them to Marren Motorsports and have them blueprinted. Do you have a clogged exhaust or a small vacuum leak? Are your tires under inflated? Do you have fat oversized tires? Tires have a noticeable effect on gas mileage. Are your brakes dragging? Get out of the car and feel for excess heat in the wheels on all corners. Is your transmission lockup working (automatic)? Don't put a used coolant temperature sensor on your car when a new one costs less than $10. Is your MAP sensor going south even though you have no codes?<P>Check this stuff!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||09-09-2000||09:20 PM||||So a cracked exhaust manifold would cause a code 32?? <P>I keep getting this code too and my front manifold developed a leak.....I guess if the two are related I need to fix that manifold!||||reg||5
Z||000004||Vlad||09-09-2000||10:25 PM||||I will try to answer.<P>&gt;Does your car have good vacuum, 18-20 inches at idle? <P>To be honest, I don't know what you are talking about. How do I check? The idle  in my Fiero is 850-1000 rpm when engine is hot.<P>&gt;Do you have an exhaust manifold leak?<P>No. It seems to be fine. <P>&gt;Are your injectors clogged and leaking? <P>I was thinking about them. Is there any way to check them without disassembling the top of the engine?<P>Do you have a clogged exhaust or a small vacuum leak?<P>Checked. Doesn't seem to be clogged. BTW, car is not underpowered.<P>&gt;Are your tires under inflated? <BR>&gt;Do you have fat oversized tires?<P>I have 235/60 R14. I keep them in 33 pci.<BR> <BR>&gt;Are your brakes dragging?<P>Checked. No eccessive heat from wheels.<P>&gt;Is your transmission lockup working (automatic)?<P>I put a new one due to the hot stalling.<P>&gt;Is your MAP sensor going south even though you have no codes?<P>Don't know. How do I check it for proper operation?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
